- Dates constructed from ISO week components often format with year "0000".
- iso_week().year() returns 0 where it should return the ISO year (e.g. 2001).
- Parsing/formatting helpers that depend on ISO-week calculations can return parse errors ("impossible") or incorrect values.
- Some min/max getters that depend on ISO-week internals return incorrect sentinel/min values instead of expected numbers.

### Expected outcome

- NaiveDate::from_isoywd and related APIs should produce correct dates (e.g. 2001-01-01).
- Formatting with "%Y" should print the correct year.
- iso_week().year() should return the ISO year (2001 in the example).
- Parsing/formatting that uses ISO week data should succeed and return expected values.

